<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">28 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">4 events that happened on 28 November, from 1520 to 1943.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/south-america" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/south-america.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1520">1520 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">506 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Magellan's ships enter the Pacific</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After 38 days navigating the strait at the tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-magellan">Ferdinand Magellan</a>'s three remaining ships reached the open ocean. He named it the Pacific for its calm waters.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1905">1905 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">121 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Arthur Griffith launches Sinn Féin's policy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At a convention in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a>, Arthur Griffith set out the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sinn-fein">Sinn Féin</a> policy, meaning 'we ourselves', of Irish self-reliance and a separate Irish parliament. The movement later became central to the struggle for independence.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1912">1912 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">114 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Albania declares independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlore">Vlorë</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismail-qemali">Ismail Qemali</a> raised the Albanian flag and proclaimed independence from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-balkan-war">First Balkan War</a>. The great powers recognised the new state the following year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1943">1943 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Churchill, Roosevelt and Stalin meet in Tehran</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The 'Big Three' met together for the first time at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tehran">Tehran</a> Conference. They committed to a cross-Channel invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1944 and discussed the shape of post-war <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p></div></li></ol>
